[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: A person cycling on a road, with "Insta360 X6" text overlay.
AUDIO: 'This intro clip was automatically generated&nbsp; by the new AI Director feature. A new feature&nbsp;&nbsp; of the X6 that automatically generates a video&nbsp; with music and effects from your footage from a&nbsp;&nbsp; single day. You don\'t even have to transfer&nbsp; your footage—just activate the feature and&nbsp;&nbsp; plug the camera in to charge. And that\'s it. For many, the need to reframe their footage&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:13] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A hand interacting with the Insta360 app on a smartphone, showing a 360-degree video preview.
AUDIO: 'is still considered the biggest drawback of a 360&nbsp; camera. And it is precisely to solve this problem&nbsp;&nbsp; that Insta360 has developed three new automated&nbsp; editing features for the launch of the X6,&nbsp;&nbsp; which are designed to take all the editing&nbsp; work off your hands. These are AutoEdit 2.0,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:28] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: The presenter holding an Insta360 camera, talking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'AI Director and Moments Pro. All three features&nbsp; will be available not only for the X6, but also&nbsp;&nbsp; for the X5; Moments Pro and AutoEdit 2.0 will&nbsp; also be available for other Insta 360 cameras.&nbsp;&nbsp; As the sheer number of features can quickly become&nbsp; confusing, today I’ll show you how these three&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'features work and what the differences are. It’s worth bearing in mind that the Insta360&nbsp;&nbsp; app also provides several tools for the actual&nbsp; reframing process, which automate the process.&nbsp;&nbsp; For example, you can have the app analyse the clip&nbsp; and then simply select a perspective. Or you can&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let the app decide what the optimal perspective&nbsp; might be. But in all these cases, you have to&nbsp;&nbsp; open the clip in the app, make a selection&nbsp; and then export it. All three new features&nbsp;&nbsp; are designed to take this work off your hands. AutoEdit 2.0 is essentially an improved version&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:14] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone displaying a gallery of video clips within the Insta360 app.
AUDIO: 'of the existing AutoEdit feature. You select&nbsp; a few clips in the app; the app analyses them,&nbsp;&nbsp; adds filters, transitions and music, and creates&nbsp; a ready-made montage of your selected clips – all&nbsp;&nbsp; completely automatically. Once it’s finished,&nbsp; you can then change the template – there are&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'loads of templates to choose from. You can also&nbsp; adjust the length if the app has captured enough&nbsp;&nbsp; highlights. If needed, you can edit the montage&nbsp; yourself; you can change the order of the clips,&nbsp;&nbsp; the transitions, the music – pretty much&nbsp; everything. Of all three features we’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be looking at today, AutoEdit 2.0 gives you the&nbsp; most control. Compared to the previous version,&nbsp;&nbsp; the feature has been significantly improved.&nbsp; There are hardly any pointless angles or&nbsp;&nbsp; unnecessary clips in the finished video. Moments Pro and AI Director are also about&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'creating an automated montage from multiple&nbsp; clips, but the approach is completely different.&nbsp;&nbsp; AI Director is a further development of the AI&nbsp; Highlights Assistant. And it needs to be activated&nbsp;&nbsp; in the camera. With the feature activated, you&nbsp; then take a series of clips throughout the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'switch off the camera at the end of the day and&nbsp; plug it in to charge. As soon as the battery&nbsp;&nbsp; reaches 80 per cent, the AI Director kicks in. It&nbsp; captures the highlights from that day’s footage,&nbsp;&nbsp; creates a custom-generated clip and automatically&nbsp; transfers it to your smartphone. If you want to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'save time, you can also set the camera&nbsp; to capture highlights while recording.&nbsp; This speeds up the process and makes&nbsp; it possible to produce the daily vlog&nbsp;&nbsp; more quickly, but it also uses up energy. With the AI Director Everything is fully automated&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and you don’t need to select any clips yourself.&nbsp; The compilation consists of the clips from a&nbsp;&nbsp; single day. Depending on your settings, you’ll&nbsp; receive a notification from the app as soon as the&nbsp;&nbsp; video is ready, allowing you to view that day’s&nbsp; highlights effortlessly. If you’ve disabled push&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:57] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone showing the "Memories" section in the Insta360 app, displaying AI Director-generated videos.
AUDIO: 'notifications, you’ll find the daily vlogs under&nbsp; ‘Memories’. This feature requires only the camera&nbsp;&nbsp; and the app – no data is transferred to the cloud. And that’s the key difference to Moments and&nbsp;&nbsp; Moments Pro. These are cloud-based features, for&nbsp; which you naturally need a cloud subscription. You&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:12] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone displaying the "Moments Pro" section in the Insta360 app with suggested video ideas.
AUDIO: 'can think of Moments Pro as a sort of editing&nbsp; assistant. Based on the clips you’ve uploaded&nbsp;&nbsp; to the cloud, Moments automatically suggests&nbsp; specific video ideas – and all you have to do&nbsp;&nbsp; is decide whether you actually want to&nbsp; put them into practice. Alternatively,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:27] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone showing the "Moments Pro" interface with a ready video and credit information.
AUDIO: 'you can also set tasks yourself and select&nbsp; specific keywords. For example, the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp; the scene or the recording mode. Moments Pro will&nbsp; then search through your footage for cycling clips&nbsp;&nbsp; or travel clips, for instance. The advantage of&nbsp; this is that even older, perhaps long-forgotten&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A smartphone displaying the "Smart Cloud Library" in the Insta360 app, showing various video clips.
AUDIO: 'recordings could be taken into account – or, much like with AutoEdit, you can select the&nbsp;&nbsp; clips yourself and then specify the aspect ratio,&nbsp; duration and style. And then start the edit. The&nbsp;&nbsp; whole process now takes place in the cloud, and&nbsp; you’ll be notified as soon as the clip is ready.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here in the overview, you’ll find the finished&nbsp; clips, which you can download or share. I got&nbsp;&nbsp; the impression that the Moments Pro results tend&nbsp; to use the most striking styles and filters – for&nbsp;&nbsp; example, a strong retro look. Some of the finished&nbsp; clips look really cool and professional. On the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other hand, the clips are currently in 1080p,&nbsp; so they’re of reduced quality and are therefore&nbsp;&nbsp; mainly suitable for social media. Moments&nbsp; Pro requires a cloud subscription and an&nbsp;&nbsp; additional subscription for a certain number of&nbsp; edits. However, the standard cloud subscription&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'does include a few individual Moments clips for&nbsp; specific events. Insta360 calls this Moments Lite.&nbsp; I hope that was all clear and straightforward.&nbsp; Drop me a comment if you have any further&nbsp;&nbsp; questions. The X6 is coming out in 2 days.&nbsp; There’ll be a detailed review and, if you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'interested in getting the X6, you can certainly&nbsp; expect another special offer on this channel. So&nbsp;&nbsp; give me a like as feedback if you found the video&nbsp; interesting. Stay tuned and see you next time!'
